course: dictionary
lesson: 9641
title: Stupidity and silly acts
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Stupidity is a noun, from the word stupid. It means not thinking well or not understanding something. It can also mean a silly or foolish act or idea, so look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: «an act of stupidity» names one foolish thing that someone did. In a safety lesson, people warn that a moment of stupidity, like playing near railway lines, can cause an accident. Here stupidity means a careless choice that could be dangerous.
explain: Stupidity is a strong word. Calling a person stupid is unkind, so it is better to describe the action instead. A different way of speaking is not stupidity either: «I seen him at the chippy» is dialect, which many people use.
fact: Stupidity means not thinking well, or not understanding.
fact: A stupidity is a silly or foolish act or idea, as in «an act of stupidity».
fact: «Stupidity» is a strong word; calling a person stupid is unkind.
fact: A moment of stupidity, like playing near railway lines, can cause an accident.
fact: Dialect is a way of speaking used in one place, like «I seen him at the chippy»; it is not stupidity.
exercise: In «an act of stupidity», what is stupidity? | A type of weather | A kind thing someone did | A long journey | *A silly or foolish act
exercise: Why is calling a person stupid unkind? | Stupid people are never kind | It means the same as clever | *It is a strong insult that hurts people | It is a long word
exercise: Which of these is dialect, not stupidity? | «The bus was late again» | «He forgot his coat» | «Playing near railway lines is dangerous» | *«I seen him at the chippy»
test: What does stupidity mean? | A kind and gentle mood | A very fast way to run | *Not thinking well, or not understanding | A tasty snack
test: What should you do instead of calling someone stupid? | Tell them they are a stupidity | Laugh and walk away | Shout at them loudly | *Describe the silly action, not the person
exam: Which sentence uses stupidity correctly for a silly act? | *The driver's stupidity on the icy road nearly caused a crash | The stupidity of the bus was bright yellow | Stupidity is the name of a sunny day | Stupidity is a fast horse that runs in the park
